  <element>
    <id>Text</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>75</x>
      <y>345</y>
      <w>1170</w>
      <h>155</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>[synthesis failure] AI_UNAVAILABLE; report=null; no invented recommendation.
REQUEST_BUILD: local prompt/schema construction failed before a request.
LLMFailure.diagnostic(): configuration / timeout / HTTP / provider envelope.
REQUEST_FAILURE: unclassified client/request exception (details withheld).
REPORT_STRUCTURE: parseReport rejected JSON, fields, types, bounds or category.
REPORT_EVIDENCE: validateReport rejected evidence or supported prose claims.
fontsize=24
halign=left
bg=white</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>55</x>
      <y>540</y>
      <w>1220</w>
      <h>65</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>EvaluationReport = content; ReportEvidence = authoritative context; ReportEvaluation
= generation/status envelope. AI_UNAVAILABLE and insufficient states are cacheable too.
fontsize=24
bg=white</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLFrame</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1350</x>
      <y>110</y>
      <w>1330</w>
      <h>510</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>sd B2 — accepted categories and exact validation boundaries
fontsize=24</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1380</x>
      <y>160</y>
      <w>1250</w>
      <h>85</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Four advisory categories: Strong Candidate · Consider with Caution · High Risk
· Insufficient Information. Category and generation status are separate concepts.
Strong Candidate additionally needs sufficient evidence, no violations, Low risk and a first-year estimate.
fontsize=24
bg=white</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1380</x>
      <y>260</y>
      <w>1250</w>
      <h>115</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>ReportSchema: category, strengths, risks, missingInformation, costSummary,
constraintConflicts, inspectionPriorities, nextSteps, explanation. No extra properties.
Parser: strict bounded JSON; string sections; no duplicate keys/items; valid category.
Exact costSummary; supported strengths subset; five required evidence sets unchanged.
fontsize=24
bg=white</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1380</x>
      <y>390</y>
      <w>1250</w>
      <h>110</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Narrative validator checks covered accident/maintenance claims clause by clause.
NO cannot become reported accidents; DOCUMENTED is not missing or complete history.
Then reject digits, prohibited age/condition terms and covered constraint contradictions.
These are targeted English guards, not universal factual or mechanical verification.
fontsize=24
bg=white</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>Text</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1380</x>
      <y>535</y>
      <w>1250</w>
      <h>65</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>All failures retain Java evidence. No automatic corrective or F09 transient retry.
Costs/constraints remain Java facts; prior risk and final category remain AI interpretations.
fontsize=24
halign=left
bg=white</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
